I know exactly why this crashed! You copied the fantastic "Workflow Timeline" UI from your **Voucher Authorization** screen over to your **Voucher Posting Status** screen (which is a great idea to keep the UI consistent).
However, you accidentally copied two variables that **do not exist** in the VoucherPostingStatus.jsx file: isEscalated and viewingBatch.
Because React cannot find those variables defined anywhere in this file, it instantly crashes the moment you click "View & actions".
Here is the exact fix.
### The Fix
Scroll down to the very bottom of your VoucherPostingStatus.jsx file, inside the <Dialog> where the Stepper is mapping through the dynamicSteps.
Look for this specific block of code (around line 1558):
```javascript
{/* Keep existing Pending Since logic for the current stage (hide for System execution) */}
{isCurrent && viewingBatchState !== "REJECTED" && step.role !== "System" && (
  <Typography variant="caption" display="block" color={isEscalated ? "warning.main" : "text.secondary"} fontWeight="bold" sx={{ mt: 0.5 }}>
    Pending Since: {viewingBatch?.timeSinceLastAction || "0h 0m"}
  </Typography>
)}

```
**Replace that entire block with this corrected version:**
```javascript
{/* Keep existing Pending Since logic for the current stage (hide for System execution) */}
{isCurrent && viewingBatchState !== "REJECTED" && step.role !== "System" && (
  <Typography variant="caption" display="block" color="text.secondary" fontWeight="bold" sx={{ mt: 0.5 }}>
    Pending Since: {viewingBatchTimeSinceLastAction || "0h 0m"}
  </Typography>
)}

```
### Why this fixes it:
 1. **Removed isEscalated:** The isEscalated variable is specific to the Checker's Authorization screen. For the standard Status view, we just fall back to the standard "text.secondary" color.
 2. **Fixed viewingBatch:** On the Authorization screen, your state object is called viewingBatch. On this Status screen, you split it into separate variables, so the correct state name is viewingBatchTimeSinceLastAction.
Save the file, and your modal will open perfectly!
